<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abencerrajes</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Banu Sarraj</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abencerrajes (Banu Sarraj) were a noble family of the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> who were influential at court in the fifteenth century. They acted as kingmakers in the civil wars among Nasrid claimants, notably supporting Muhammad IX, and their rivalries with other clans weakened the emirate. Legend holds that many of them were killed in a hall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhambra">Alhambra</a> that bears their name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abencerrajes.jpg" alt="Abencerrajes" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ignacio Merino · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_%C3%BAltimo_abencerraje.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
